# Folding a plane into a torus
## Technique

The surface starts as a rectangular point grid. Two families of rotations bend that grid around perpendicular axes; the controls vary the logarithms of the bend scales, so the effective values are $l_1 = 10^x$ and $l_2 = 10^{x_2}$. Larger values produce a gentler fold.

Instead of giving every quad its own four coordinates, the code flattens the grid into one shared vertex list. Each neighboring $2 \times 2$ block becomes an indexed quad face, and `GraphicsComplex` joins those faces into a single mesh. This keeps the topology explicit, avoids duplicated vertices, and is a natural representation for a connected surface.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
# Folding a plane into a torus
## Technique

The surface starts as a rectangular point grid. Two families of rotations bend that grid around perpendicular axes; the controls vary the logarithms of the bend scales, so the effective values are $l_1 = 10^x$ and $l_2 = 10^{x_2}$. Larger values produce a gentler fold.

Instead of giving every quad its own four coordinates, the code flattens the grid into one shared vertex list. Each neighboring $2 \times 2$ block becomes an indexed quad face, and `GraphicsComplex` joins those faces into a single mesh. This keeps the topology explicit, avoids duplicated vertices, and is a natural representation for a connected surface.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Manipulate[
 Module[{l = 10.^x, l2 = 10.^x2, grid, tiles, vertices, faces, rows, columns},
  grid[a_, b_, n_, m_] := Outer[
    Compose,
    Array[RotationTransform[# Pi/b, {0, 0, 1.}, {0, -b, 0}] &, n, {-1, 1}],
    Array[RotationTransform[# Pi/a, {1., 0, 0}, {0, 2, a}][{0, 2, 0}] &, m, {-1, 1}],
    1
  ];

  tiles = grid[l, l2, 50, 25];
  {rows, columns} = Dimensions[tiles][[{1, 2}]];
  vertices = Flatten[tiles, 1];
  faces = Flatten[
    Table[
     With[{i = (r - 1) columns + c}, {i, i + 1, i + columns + 1, i + columns}],
     {r, rows - 1}, {c, columns - 1}
    ],
    1
  ];

  Graphics3D[
   {Blue, GraphicsComplex[vertices, Polygon[faces]]},
   PlotRange -> {{-7, 7}, {-7, 7}, {-1, 2}},
   ImageSize -> 600,
   Axes -> True
  ]
 ],
 {{x, 2., "log10 l1"}, .0001, 2.},
 {{x2, 2., "log10 l2"}, .0001, 2.},
 ContinuousAction -> True
]

